==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 25~30 seconds<sup>750f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Lazer (Enemy)|Dark Lazer]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 18~20 seconds<sup>540f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 45~50 seconds<sup>1,350f~1,500f</sup>.
**8 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.67~5.33 seconds<sup>20f~160f</sup>.
**8 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 0.67~5.33 seconds<sup>20f~160f</sup>.
**8 [[Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 44 seconds<sup>1,320f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be very difficult without [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] because the Gory Darks and Doge Darks can break through your defenses easily, especially when the boss comes out. Dark Lazer attacks relentlessly and has a great deal of staying power; fortunately, she is considered a [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy, which allows you to use abilities such as [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Eastwood]]'s slow, [[Tin Cat (Rare Cat)|Plane Cat]]'s knockback, etc. to slow or entirely stop her advance. Using the [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] is not recommended because you need to be very aware of what's being sent out – a single Gory Dark, if not dealt with properly, could tear through your defenses and allow the boss to advance.

